  (https://github.com/commenthol/date-holidays), with its date-holidays-parser
  package. Their code is under the ISC license. The holiday data in
  date-holidays (data/holidays.json and data/countries/*.yaml), mostly from
  Wikipedia articles, is under Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike: the
  package declares CC-BY-SA-4.0 (package.json, LICENSE, holidays.json), while
  its README and the attribution list in its LICENSE file name CC BY-SA 3.0,
  the license of the Wikipedia text it was taken from. The attribution (the
  source articles) is in the package's LICENSE file. Linedesk does not include
  this data in the repository; it comes with the package.

